    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0349" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Hsu
                            Yung-chang to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-23">23 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the pleasure to inform you that his Excellency, The Generalissimo, has
                    appointed me as acting representative for the National Government on the
                    Sub-Committee of Three. Representatives of the Chinese Communist Party are, too,
                    being informed of the matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hsu Yung-Chang</hi></signed> (<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>)<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Government
                        Representative,</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sub-Committee of
                    Three</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
